  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes typecheck. I haven't built it with `vite build` or run it in a browser, so I haven't checked how the framing, shadow or crossfade look.\n\nThe scene loads `/assets/soldier.glb`, scaled to a height of 1.8. It plays `Idle` on start, with a perspective camera aimed at the character. The ground is a plane, and one directional light casts the shadow, plus a hemisphere light for fill. `R` cross-fades to `Run` and `I` cross-fades back to `Idle`, each over 0.4 seconds. `window.__EVAL__.clip()` returns the target clip as soon as a key is pressed.\n\n`window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the first `requestAnimationFrame` after `app.ready()` resolves.\n\nI copied the soldier asset's sha256 and the scene setup from the project's `recipes.md`. I did not compute the hash myself.",
